Task 2
      What is the difference between IPv4 and IPv6? Answer in 2 lines. 
Answer
      IPv4  
          uses a 32-bit address and provides about 4.3 billion addresses, e.g., 192.168.1.1. 
      IPv6  
          uses a 128-bit address and provides a much larger number of addresses, e.g., 2001:db8::1.


