Task 4
      What do these HTTP status codes mean: 200, 301, 404, 500, 403? 
Answer
      Code Meaning                  Explanation
      200 OK                        Request was successful. 
      301 Moved Permanently         The requested resource has permanently moved to another URL. 
      404 Not Found                 The requested page or resource could not be found. 
      500 Internal Server Error     An unexpected error occurred on the server. 
      403 Forbidden                 The server understood the request but refuses to allow access.

Task 5
      Explain DNS hierarchy (root, TLD, domain, subdomain) with www.google.com as an example. 
Answer
      DNS hierarchy works from Root → TLD → Domain → Subdomain. 
          For www.google.com: 
            Root (.) → The top level of the DNS hierarchy.  
            TLD (.com) → The Top-Level Domain.  
            Domain (google) → The registered domain name.  
            Subdomain (www) → A subdomain/hostname used to iden fy a par cular service or web server.  
      So, the hierarchy is: 
      Root (.) → TLD (com) → Domain (google) → Subdomain (www).
